---
/**
 * @license MIT
 * ============================================================================
 * src/pages/commercial-licensing.astro — B2B Sync Licensing (`/commercial-licensing`)
 * ============================================================================
 * PLAIN-ENGLISH OVERVIEW (100-LEVEL JAVASCRIPT & ASTRO 6 GUIDE):
 * What is this file?
 *   Astro 6 file-based route blueprint for `/commercial-licensing`.
 *
 * How does it fit into the build lifecycle?
 *   - Route Blueprint: Declares the page title, meta description, and canonical
 *     URL path inside the build-time `---` frontmatter and `BaseLayout` wrapper.
 *   - Static Compilation: `scripts/build.mjs` invokes `renderCommercialLicensingPage()`
 *     from `src/renderers/pages-artists-and-legal.mjs` to emit
 *     `./dist/commercial-licensing/index.html`.
 *
 * What visible UI does `/commercial-licensing` produce?
 *   Explains Engine Room Records' dual-track licensing model in plain language:
 *   1. Free / Open Culture Tier: All 128kbps web MP3 streams and ZIP archives on
 *      `music.raggiesoft.com` are free under Creative Commons BY-SA 4.0.
 *   2. Proprietary B2B Sync Tier: One-stop commercial synchronization clearance
 *      for film, TV, video games, and broadcast productions that cannot use
 *      ShareAlike terms or need uncompressed 24-bit WAV studio stems.
 * ============================================================================
 */

// Import the shared HTML5 shell component at build time.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<!-- Wrap `/commercial-licensing` metadata inside BaseLayout's outer document frame -->
<BaseLayout
  title="Commercial Synchronization Licensing | Engine Room Records"
  description="Non-exclusive commercial synchronization clearances for Film, TV, Games, and Broadcast across the Engine Room Records catalog."
  canonicalPath="/commercial-licensing"
>
  <!-- Dual-track licensing cards compiled via renderCommercialLicensingPage() in scripts/build.mjs -->
</BaseLayout>
